                            "type": "TRANSLATION_LITERAL",
                            "value": {
                                "code": null,
                                "comment": "",
                                "message": "<p data-end=\"633\" data-start=\"346\">An Authenticator App is a mobile application that generates time-based one-time passcodes (OTP) used as a second step in Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA). After entering their password, users retrieve a temporary 6-digit code from the app and enter it to complete the login process.</p>\n<h4 data-end=\"657\" data-start=\"635\"><strong>How It Works</strong>:</h4>\n<ol>\n<li data-end=\"657\" data-start=\"635\">The user links their account to an authenticator app (e.g.,&nbsp;<em data-end=\"781\" data-start=\"721\">Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator, Okta Verify</em>).</li>\n<li data-end=\"657\" data-start=\"635\">During login, they enter their password and retrieve a code from the app.</li>\n<li data-end=\"657\" data-start=\"635\">The code changes every 30 seconds, ensuring it&rsquo;s unique and time-sensitive for each login attempt.</li>\n</ol>\n<h4 data-end=\"978\" data-start=\"964\">Advantages:</h4>\n<ul>\n<li data-end=\"978\" data-start=\"964\">More secure than SMS or email OTPs (not vulnerable to SIM swapping or interception).</li>\n<li data-end=\"978\" data-start=\"964\">Works offline&mdash;does not require an active internet connection.</li>\n<li data-end=\"978\" data-start=\"964\">Free, widely supported, and easy to set up across multiple platforms.</li>\n</ul>"
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "slot": null,
                    "styles": null
                }
